The saying dates back to at least to WWII and was used by soldiers, sailors,
marines, etc to describe the situations they were in.  It was used very
disparagingly, as the general consensus (sp?) was that they were in these
situations because of a decision made by somebody higher up in the chain
of command, who was presumably there because he was smarter or more exper-
ienced than those who ended up in these situations.  Maybe he was, as he
(usually) was not in those situations with them. ;-)
